  <h1>Join the Group</h1>

  <p>
    <strong>
      I am recruiting M.Sc. and Ph.D. students to start January or September 2027. Funded positions are available.
    </strong>
    Students join the Department of Earth, Energy &amp; Environment at the
    University of Calgary through the thesis-based
    <a href="https://grad.ucalgary.ca/future-students/graduate/discover-opportunities/explore-programs/geoscience-msc-thesis">M.Sc.</a>
    or
    <a href="https://grad.ucalgary.ca/future-students/graduate/discover-opportunities/explore-programs/geoscience-phd">Ph.D.</a>
    programs in Geoscience.
  </p>

  <hr />

  <h2>Please email me if you are interested in applying</h2>

  <p>
    Send me a message at
    <a href="mailto:chance.ronemus@ucalgary.ca">chance.ronemus@ucalgary.ca</a>
    with:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>A short note about your research interests</li>
    <li>Your CV</li>
    <li>An unofficial transcript</li>
    <li>Whether you are aiming for an M.Sc. or a Ph.D.</li>
    <li>Your target start term</li>
  </ul>

  <hr />

  <h2>What you would work on</h2>

  <p>
    My group studies how mountain belts grow and how their sedimentary basins
    record that growth, combining field geology with detrital zircon
    geochronology, igneous petrochronology, and stable isotope geochemistry.
    More detail is on my <a href="/research-projects/">research page</a>.
    If you have an idea that connects to these, feel free to tell me about
    it.
  </p>

  <hr />

  <h2>What the work is like</h2>

  <p>
    Most projects involve a field season followed by lab work and data analysis. You
    should genuinely want to spend time in the mountains, and be prepared for fieldwork.
    I care more about curiosity, persistence, and care with data than about a
    perfect transcript. 
    </p>

    <p>
    Students in my group present at national meetings, lead
    their own papers, and get trained on the analytical instruments. You can see what previous
    students have done on my
    <a href="/teaching/">research group page</a>.
  </p>

  <hr />

  <h2>Funding</h2>

  <p>
    Funded positions are available, and I will be explicit about the
    funding attached to any project before you apply. Students are also
    encouraged to apply for external awards like NSERC Canada Graduate
    Scholarships (for Canadian citizens and permanent residents), and internal awards at the
    University of Calgary.
  </p>

  <hr />

  <h2>Undergraduates at Calgary</h2>

  <p>
    I am also anticipating work with undergraduate researchers, and I am glad to talk with Calgary
    students about honours theses, summer research, and field opportunities.
    Email me with what you are interested in and where you are in your degree.
  </p>

  <p>
    <a class="button" href="mailto:chance.ronemus@ucalgary.ca">Email me</a>
  </p>
